    "description": "<p>We explicitly answer the mixed point-spectrum converse left open after Theorem 3.1.14(i) of Kari Valentina Kuster's 2015 thesis and stated only as an inclusion in her 2016 Pure Koopmanism contribution. For a matrix contraction on a finite-dimensional complex space with any complex norm, acting by composition on all continuous complex functions on its closed unit ball, every unimodular eigenfunction factors through the contractive peripheral spectral projection. The unimodular point spectrum is exactly the multiplicative group generated by the peripheral matrix eigenvalues. An elementary self-contained proof yields the full point and Banach-operator spectrum classification, including singular, nilpotent and nonnormal cases.</p><p>The missing exclusion is a short specialization of classical Jacobs-de Leeuw-Glicksberg theory and the prior all-peripheral calculation. The open-disk eigenvalues, prior peripheral and nilpotent cases, and the already immediate full-disk consequence are explicitly credited. A bounded primary-source audit found no earlier explicit completion in the examined scope; source-edition and coverage gaps are documented. No worldwide firstness, exhaustive literature absence, continuous 2015-2026 openness, new general decomposition theorem, or novel full-disk spectrum is claimed.</p><p>AI tools were used extensively in solving, drafting, reproducing and adversarially reviewing this work. This is an unrefereed preprint without conventional human peer review. The package includes the PDF and LaTeX source, a portable verification archive with recorded results and provenance, a priority supplement, instructions, license and digests. The 2720 finite controls per mode include 566 floating diagnostics; repetition under ordinary and optimized Python does not increase the number of distinct controls. Finite controls supplement the analytic proof and do not certify an infinite-dimensional spectrum or historical priority.</p>"
  },
